# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The IDE, closed end to end: the editor is handed a program through
# the shell's panel, colours it because its name says BASIC, and RUNS
# it -- in the interpreter a BOARD runs, the kernel's own engine
# compiled for the host, as a child on the far end of a pipe.  The
# program's effect lands in a real file beside its source, which is
# the one claim a test can hold in its hand.
wait 14
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/blink.bas
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
click 60 8
wait 6
menu-pick Open…
wait 30
expect-title Open
note the program is picked in the shell's own panel
click 400 262
wait 4
click 675 413
wait 40
expect-no-title Open
note Run is offered because the NAME said BASIC, and taking it runs
note the program on the board's own interpreter
click-window Edit
wait 4
click 60 8
wait 6
expect-menu Run
menu-pick Run
wait 120
note the run's effect is in the sandbox beside the source: the lamp
note file holds what the program wrote
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/led 7
note and what the program SAID is in the output pane, in the ink that
note tells a reader these words came from the run rather than the file
expect-pixel 233 374 607060
note put the editor away
click-window Edit
wait 4
key Escape
wait 30
quit
